    {
      "post_id": 36769,
      "author_username": "alexintx",
      "author_user_id": 993,
      "timestamp_iso": "2018-04-06T02:34:23+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1522982063000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Apr 5, 2018 21:34:23 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "These photos are all from the first. We've had enough cloudy days that the color on my plants isn't quite as nice as it could be, but that won't be a problem for too long. This'll probably be my last batch of photos until I get back home for the summer.<br/>First up is the sarr I've had for longest:<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/GdmWL8\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/787/26394155127_70cc8f390b_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><br/>The pitchers look pretty nice, but it looks like the top of the flower bud was chewed on by something, and it has stopped growing.<br/><br/>My new <i>S. rosea</i> was the last one to start coming out of dormancy:<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25NEjdY\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/892/41222153992_06152bb03d_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><br/><br/>My flytraps look nice, as always:<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25NEjis\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/873/41222154252_ba79ddb910_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><br/><br/>This little guy bit off more than he could chew:<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/GdmX2t\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/784/26394156017_0f6e9640cb_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><br/><br/>One of the growth points from the sarr that started to rot has begun to open its pitcher:<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/GdmXbg\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/868/26394156527_22f80d1fea_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a><br/><br/>And last is the rhizome chunk I got in the rhizome sale. I was worried because it had no growth points, but that's clearly not a problem anymore:<br/><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25NEjqw\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/790/41222154662_8e0e9f2c01_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;\"/></a>",
      "body_text": "These photos are all from the first. We've had enough cloudy days that the color on my plants isn't quite as nice as it could be, but that won't be a problem for too long. This'll probably be my last batch of photos until I get back home for the summer.\nFirst up is the sarr I've had for longest:\nThe pitchers look pretty nice, but it looks like the top of the flower bud was chewed on by something, and it has stopped growing.\nMy new\nS. rosea\nwas the last one to start coming out of dormancy:\nMy flytraps look nice, as always:\nThis little guy bit off more than he could chew:\nOne of the growth points from the sarr that started to rot has begun to open its pitcher:\nAnd last is the rhizome chunk I got in the rhizome sale. I was worried because it had no growth points, but that's clearly not a problem anymore:",
