    {
      "post_id": 36874,
      "author_username": "rmeyer",
      "author_user_id": 249,
      "timestamp_iso": "2018-04-15T17:00:25+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1523811625000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Apr 15, 2018 12:00:25 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "<span itemscope=\"\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\"><a class=\"user-link js-user-link user-963 group-0\" href=\"/user/963\" itemprop=\"url\" title=\"@atroviridis\"><span itemprop=\"name\">atroviridis</span></a></span> <br/>South Dakota? And I thought I had a disadvantage. How long have you grown sarracenia in South Dakota?<br/><br/><br/><span itemscope=\"\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\"><a class=\"user-link js-user-link user-993 group-0\" href=\"/user/993\" itemprop=\"url\" title=\"@alexintx\"><span itemprop=\"name\">alexintx</span></a></span> <br/>Your situation should improve this week. As will mine.<br/><br/>My plants will come out of the garage tomorrow after work to a transitional area. If it doesn't freeze during the week they'll be good to go for the season. Probably won't hold my breath, though. ",
      "body_text": "atroviridis\nSouth Dakota? And I thought I had a disadvantage. How long have you grown sarracenia in South Dakota?\nalexintx\nYour situation should improve this week. As will mine.\nMy plants will come out of the garage tomorrow after work to a transitional area. If it doesn't freeze during the week they'll be good to go for the season. Probably won't hold my breath, though.",
